<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jiang Zemin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1926–2022</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jiang Zemin was a Chinese Communist leader who became general secretary of the party after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1989-tiananmen-square-protests-and-massacre">Tiananmen Square protests</a> of 1989 and served as president of the People's Republic from 1993 to 2003. His years in power saw rapid market-oriented growth, the return of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macau">Macau</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>'s entry into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/world-trade-organization">World Trade Organization</a> in 2001.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jiang-zemin.jpg" alt="Jiang Zemin" width="320" height="425" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The Presidential Press and Information Office · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:President_Jiang_Zemin_2002.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
